# .pzstudioignore example
#
# This file controls what PZStudio skips when it scaffolds or builds content
# from a template or project tree.
#
# Rules:
# - One pattern per line.
# - Blank lines are ignored.
# - Lines starting with `#` are comments.
# - Paths are matched relative to the directory that contains this file.
# - Use `/` for folders. A trailing `/` is optional.
#
# Built-in exclusions already handled by PZStudio:
# - `.gitkeep`
# - `.git`
# - `.github`
# - `.gitmodules`
#
# Notes for this codebase:
# - `pzstudio new` copies the project template, mod template, workshop template,
#   and shared folders like `.libraries`.
# - `pzstudio build` also ignores dotfiles in copied output, except
#   `.pzstudioignore` itself.
# - Nested `.pzstudioignore` files are supported. The closest file wins.

# Keep local editor metadata out of generated output
.vscode/
.idea/
.fleet/

# Keep generated or packaged files out of templates and builds
dist/
build/
out/
coverage/
*.log

# Keep local cache and temporary files out of the scaffold
.cache/
.temp/
tmp/

# Ignore optional local-only mod resources
screenshots/
notes/

# Example: ignore one file
README-draft.md

# Example: ignore a nested folder in a mod or shared folder
assets/generated/

